      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i just updated the A records for our client's site but the new IP isnt showing up for me yet. why does it take so long for dns changes to actually work everywhere?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The delay you're experiencing is called DNS propagation, and it's a completely normal part of how the internet works. It takes time because DNS records are cached by various servers all over the world. Think of it like a massive, decentralized network of little digital filing cabinets that need to update their information before everyone sees the change. You just need to be patient while these caches refresh!",
