    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay so if it's just caching that's the main thing? i'm seeing some locations seeing the old IP and others seeing the new one. is there any way to speed it up or do we just have to wait for the ttl to expire?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, caching is the primary reason for the inconsistency you're seeing—some servers haven't refreshed their memory yet. You can't truly *force* the change everywhere instantly, because that would require every single server on the planet to update at the exact same moment, which is impossible. The Time To Live (TTL) is the mechanism that dictates how long those servers are allowed to keep the old information before checking for a new one.\n\nIf you need to expedite things, the only real way is to lower the TTL *before* making the change in the first place, so that when you update the A record, the waiting period is much shorter. Otherwise, you're just waiting for the existing TTLs to naturally expire across the globe.",
